/T (Low-cost systems enable non-state actors, smaller nations, and proxy forces to execute precision strikes, conduct real-time reconnaissance, and overwhelm traditional air defense networks. This democratization of aerial strike capabilities poses severe challenges to traditional arms control regimes, export control standards, and the tracking of dual-use technology supply chains.)
/E (Low-cost systems enable non-state actors, smaller nations, and proxy forces to execute precision strikes, conduct real-time reconnaissance, and overwhelm traditional air defense networks. This democratization of aerial strike capabilities poses severe challenges to traditional arms control regimes, export control standards, and the tracking of dual-use technology supply chains.)
