>>
endobj
410 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 117 0 R
/T (Modern arms control developed significantly during the Cold War, when the United States and Soviet Union sought to manage the dangers created by their nuclear arsenals.)
/E (Modern arms control developed significantly during the Cold War, when the United States and Soviet Union sought to manage the dangers created by their nuclear arsenals.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
411 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 117 0 R
/T (Treaties such as the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty, Strategic Arms Limitation Talks, Intermediate-Range Nuclear Forces Treaty, and New START created different forms of limitations, transparency, and verification.)
/E (Treaties such as the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty, Strategic Arms Limitation Talks, Intermediate-Range Nuclear Forces Treaty, and New START created different forms of limitations, transparency, and verification.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
412 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 117 0 R
/T (Arms-control agreements have also addressed chemical weapons, biological weapons, conventional weapons, and weapons testing.)
/E (Arms-control agreements have also addressed chemical weapons, biological weapons, conventional weapons, and weapons testing.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
413 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 117 0 R
/T (However, the international arms-control framework has experienced significant setbacks in recent years. The United States and Russia withdrew from the Intermediate-Range Nuclear Forces Treaty in 2019, while New START expired in 2026.)
/E (However, the international arms-control framework has experienced significant setbacks in recent years. The United States and Russia withdrew from the Intermediate-Range Nuclear Forces Treaty in 2019, while New START expired in 2026.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
414 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 117 0 R
/T (These developments have increased concerns regarding strategic stability and the possibility of renewed arms competition.)
/E (These developments have increased concerns regarding strategic stability and the possibility of renewed arms competition.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
415 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 117 0 R
/T (At the same time, technological developments are creating capabilities that were not considered when many existing treaties were negotiated. This raises questions about whether traditional arms-control structures are sufficiently flexible to address modern security challenges.)
/E (At the same time, technological developments are creating capabilities that were not considered when many existing treaties were negotiated. This raises questions about whether traditional arms-control structures are sufficiently flexible to address modern security challenges.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
